/ "Undo the acceptance" on a booked receipt (Receipts::UndoAccept), below the review form: a form of its own, since
/ forms do not nest. It carries the receipt's and the transaction's versions the page shows (`version`,
/ `transaction_version`), so a page older than the last acceptance or edit undoes nothing. The service decides
/ whether the transaction is still as the acceptance left it; a transaction it can never put back (booked before
/ bookings were recorded, not created by a receipt) gets no button.
ruby:
  booking = receipt.booking
  linked = booking&.linked?
  undoable = booking || transaction.from_receipt?
  undone = linked ? "Transaction ##{transaction.id} gets back the lines, status and payee it had before." : "Transaction ##{transaction.id} is deleted, with its lines."
  confirm = "Undo the acceptance? #{undone} The receipt waits for review again; its items, their categories and its ground truth stay."
section.review-section aria-labelledby=dom_id(receipt, :undo_heading)
  h2.text-base id=dom_id(receipt, :undo_heading) Accepted into the ledger
  p.text-sm.text-ink-muted
    - if linked
      | Booked on a ledger transaction it was linked to. Undoing gives that transaction back the lines, status and payee it had before.
    - elsif undoable
      | Booked as a new expense. Undoing deletes that transaction.
    - else
      | Booked before bookings were recorded, on a transaction the receipt did not create: its earlier state is not known, so the acceptance cannot be undone here.
    - if undoable
      |  Refused when the transaction changed after the acceptance.
  - if undoable
    = ui_button_to undo_accept_receipt_path(receipt, filter.to_params), variant: :secondary, size: :sm,
      params: { lock_version: version, transaction_lock_version: transaction_version },
      form: { data: { turbo_confirm: confirm } } do
      = ui_icon "undo-2"
      span Undo the acceptance
